# Login

The card that exercises most of the format at once.

## Names in play

Three different mechanisms bring three different pages into scope here:

- `[[tokens]]` → `specs/auth/tokens.hmd`, found on the spine's first entry
- `[[shared-tokens]]` → `shared/tokens.hmd`, a **named import** under an alias
- `[[token]]` → `glossary/token.hmd`, found through the **imported search path**
  `/glossary`, which is probed after the whole spine

The two `tokens` cards would collide as a bare name, which is exactly why one of
them is imported under an alias instead.

## Flow

1. The client posts credentials.
2. On success the service issues a token — see
   [[shared-tokens#Rotation|the shared rotation window]].
3. On failure it applies [[retry-policy#Backoff]]. That name is on no spine
   entry and in no import — `/shared` contributed a single named binding, not a
   search path — so it is found by **autodiscovery**, the phase this card leaves
   enabled. Compare [[/specs/billing/invoices]], which turns that phase off and
   must import the same card explicitly.

The glossary definition, embedded by block anchor rather than restated:

